# Opt-in TLS reverse proxy for the `tls` Compose profile (#1504, part of #901).
#
# Two variables control this file, both supplied by the `caddy` and `caddy-init`
# services in ../docker-compose.prod.yml — never set them anywhere else:
#   JARVIS_TLS_HOST   the hostname or LAN IP browsers will use, e.g. moss.lan
#   JARVIS_TLS_ISSUER internal (default; a self-signed local CA) or acme
#                     (a publicly trusted certificate; the host must be
#                     reachable from the internet for ACME validation)
#
# The caddy-init service validates both values before this file is ever loaded,
# so an empty or malformed host, or an issuer other than internal/acme, stops
# the proxy from starting rather than falling back to a silent catch-all site.
#
# This file is mounted into the container read-only.
#
# Certificate material (the local CA's private key and every issued
# certificate) lives only in the caddy-data named volume. It must never be
# copied into this repository, an env file, a log line, or a pull request
# comment.
https://{$JARVIS_TLS_HOST} {
	tls {
		issuer {$JARVIS_TLS_ISSUER:internal}
	}
	reverse_proxy jarv1s:3000
}
